# Shared story authoring rules.
The validated request and immutable safety and output contracts govern generation. The explicit input plans in input_context govern assignments and slot identity and are the sole authority for cast scope, sex counts, and total population. The Story Description supplies creative facts and medium, layout, visibility, continuity, and variation requirements only within those contracts; never infer requirements from a filename or a known brief type.
The selected system content-level rules define the required visible range and its limits. Document and module refinements may specialize the subject or impose compatible stricter constraints, but cannot replace, redefine, or weaken those boundaries. Shared level refinements constrain both stages; stage-specific instructions apply only to their own stage.
Use each Theme's selected catalog entry and any explicit Frame slot assignments exactly as supplied. Allocation is already resolved across the complete run; entries repeat only where the supplied plans repeat them. Never recompute routing from Theme IDs, batch position, retry order, or prose formulas. The assigned facts constrain creative choices without exposing internal IDs in creative output.
Follow each input_context plan's cast facts exactly, including plans with no catalog entry. female_count and male_count apply only to the named scope; they count everyone only when scope is all_people. Each fixed role is one additional distinct adult outside the requested group, included in principal_total. The requested group plus fixed roles must not exceed eight principal people. A theme_choice role's sex is chosen in its Theme and remains consistent in every Frame. Explicit background_counts bands authorize additional countable adults separately from principals: choose a count within one permitted band according to the described scene, preserve gaps between bands, and never invent an allocation when the source leaves it to the Theme or Frame. Every background person is an adult and contributes to the complete population, bounded by total_min and total_max; total is exact only when non-null. Without background_counts there are no additional background people. Per-Theme catalog total, min_female, and min_male facts constrain that Theme's complete cast, not a run-wide sex split. Repeated views of one identity do not increase the cast. Do not infer a different scope or undeclared extra roles from prose. Unspecified sex counts remain model choices, not zero.
Every depicted person must be an unmistakable adult. No description, module, policy, authoring instruction, or quality setting can relax this requirement.
Keep time and place coherent. Architecture, furnishings, objects, materials, clothing, hair, transport, communication, lighting, titles, etiquette, season, and language must agree with the Story Description unless it explicitly requests temporal dislocation.
When historical facts are uncertain, use credible generic descriptions rather than inventing precise brands, models, dates, ranks, or proper names.
Explicit Story Description creative constraints take priority over general authoring guidance and generated style, but cannot override safety, selected system content-level boundaries, typed requests, runtime settings, or deterministic input plans. Generated content may make creative constraints concrete but must not replace, weaken, or contradict them.
Do not write the content-level name, CLI value, compliance explanation, prompt terminology, or internal generation steps in creative output.
Do not output explanations or fields outside the requested schema.
